5. Write a short explanation (3-4 lines) describing how your current ufw configuration would impact running a local web server (like a development server for a Zomato-style food delivery app).
=>With the current configuration, a local development web server listening on ports 80 or 443 would accept connections only from localhost (loopback is typically allowed by UFW’s before.rules). External clients could not reach it because all incoming traffic except SSH/22 is denied. 
The app itself could still make outbound HTTP/HTTPS calls (e.g., to payment gateways, maps APIs, or restaurant partner services) but would be blocked from any other outbound ports (databases on non-standard ports, custom microservices, etc.). This is a restrictive “SSH + web-client only” stance suitable for a locked-down host but inconvenient for full-stack local development that needs broader inbound access or non-HTTP outbound traffic.
